{number: 88}
{title: My Jesus, As Thou Wilt!}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [C] Jesus, as Thou [F] wilt!
O [C] may Thy [G7] will be [C] mine!
Into Thy hand of [F] love
I [C] would my [G7] all re-[C] sign;
Through [G7] sorrow or through [C] joy,
Conduct me [G7] as Thine [C] own,
And help me still to [F] say,
My [C] Lord, Thy [G7] will be [C] done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [C] Jesus, as Thou [F] wilt!
Though [C] seen through [G7] many a [C] tear,
Let not my star of [F] hope
Grow [C] dim or [G7] disap-[C] pear;
Since [G7] Thou on earth hast [C] wept,
And sorrowed [G7] oft a-[C] lone,
If I must weep with [F] Thee,
My [C] Lord, Thy [G7] will be [C] done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
My [C] Jesus, as Thou [F] wilt!
All [C] shall be [G7] well for [C] me;
Each changing future [F] scene
I [C] gladly [G7] trust with [C] Thee:
Straight [G7] to my home a-[C] bove
I travel [G7] calmly [C] on,
And sing in life or [F] death,
My [C] Lord, Thy [G7] will be [C] done!
{end_of_verse}
